    "summary": "gh-918 Rework legs cannot fix CRAP/method_size/format violations — no dart toolchain in the leg env",
    "description": "Closes #918\n### Root Cause\n\nFactory legs (dev/review/rework) on Dart repos run with no Dart SDK — hosted runner images ship no `dart` and the factory setup layer had no Dart provisioner — so a rework leg cannot run `dart analyze`/`dart test`/`dart format`/`crap4dart check` and claims success while CRAP/method_size/format violations stay in place (#408, #413, #414).\n\n### Fix\n\n- `setup/dart.sh` (new): cached, channel-aware Dart SDK provisioner — same pattern as the golden-test Flutter toolchain for fa legs. Resolves the target like CI: argument/`DART_VERSION` env → the `dart-lang/setup-dart` step's `sdk:`/`channel:` in the repo's own quality workflow (\"same channel the repo's quality.yml uses\") → `stable`; downloads from the same dart-archive CDN; installs under `~/.dart-sdk/dart-sdk`; puts `bin` on PATH for the leg session + exports `DART_HOME`/`DART_VERSION`; version-aware reinstall on mismatch (persistent pool-VM `$HOME`).\n- `setup/install.sh` / `setup/cache.sh`: `dart` wired into the tool list, PATH verification, and `DART_CACHE_*` cache key/path.\n- Docs: `docs/machine-factory-integration.md` (corrected the false \"dart from the runner image\" claim, `DART_VERSION` var row), `README.md`, `scripts/warmup-session.md`. Dart-repo runners opt in via `customParams.setupCommands: [\"bash 
