Hmm wait — `rc=$?` must come IMMEDIATELY after the dart.sh line. If I insert lines between, $? breaks (echo trail_hit resets it). Fix: capture rc right after the run: change the run block to:
```js
lines.push((env...) + 'bash "$r/setup/dart.sh" ' + subcommand);
lines.push('rc=$?');
if (opts.trailTarget !== undefined) { ...compute + echo trail_hit... }
lines.push('echo "rc_line=$rc"');  // hmm — dsRun previously relied on exit $rc for cli throw
```
