Careful: stubDart also creates $d/bin — both push mkdir -p (idempotent) ✓. PATH push happens if stubDart — for stubCurlFails WITHOUT stubDart (managed case), PATH must also include $d/bin for the curl stub! Fix: push PATH when stubDart OR stubCurlFails.

Trail check opt:
```js
if (opts.trailTarget !== undefined) {
    lines.push('touch /tmp/_registered_paths');
    lines.push('before=$(wc -l < /tmp/_registered_paths)');
    // after the run:
}
```
Hmm — the run line is pushed later in dsRun (cd "$d"; env... bash dart.sh; rc). I need the trail computation AFTER the run but the run line then `rc=$?; cd /; rm -rf "$d"; exit $rc` — the sandbox dir is deleted before I can check (the trail contains $d path as a string — the file lines still exist after rm). So compute trail_hit after the run but the $d path string must be captured... after `rm -rf "$d"` the LINES in /tmp/_registered_paths still contain the old $d path text. I can compare before/after counts and grep the new lines for the literal path string saved in a var. Order: capture before, capture dpath="$d/nodart/dart-sdk/bin", run, then:
```
after=$(wc -l < /tmp/_registered_paths)
trail_hit=0
if [ "$after" -gt "$before" ]; then
  if sed -n "$((before+1)),\${p}" /tmp/_registered_paths | grep -qF "$dpath"; then trail_hit=1; fi
fi
echo "trail_hit=$trail_hit"
```
Careful with `\$p` escaping inside the JS string — write `sed -n "$((before+1)),\$p"` — in JS single-quoted string: 'sed -n "$((before+1)),$p" /tmp/_registered_paths' — the $p is inside double quotes in shell → $p would be expanded by shell as var p (empty)! Need to escape: use \\\$p? In shell, within double quotes, `\$` escapes to literal $. In JS string literal I write '\\$p' → shell sees \$p → literal $p ✓. Or avoid sed: use tail -n +N: `tail -n "+$((before+1))" /tmp/_registered_paths | grep -qF "$dpath"` — tail -n +N prints from line N onward; no $ escaping. And grep -F fixed string. But grep exit 1 when no match → guard with if.

